oss":"without thinking"},{"surface":"பின்னும்","parts":[{"text":"பின்னும்","lemma":"பின்","gloss":"again"}],"gloss":"again"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செலவு","parts":[{"text":"செலவு","lemma":"செலவு","gloss":"going"}],"gloss":"going"},{"surface":"ஆனாவே","parts":[{"text":"ஆனாவே","lemma":"ஆனா","gloss":"do not cease indeed"}],"gloss":"do not cease indeed"},{"surface":"கலிகொள்","parts":[{"text":"கலி","lemma":"கலி","gloss":"bustle"},{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"bustling"},{"surface":"புள்ளினம்","parts":[{"text":"புள்","lemma":"புள்","gloss":"bird"},{"text":"இனம்","lemma":"இனம்","gloss":"flock"}],"gloss":"flock of birds"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அனையர்","parts":[{"text":"அனையர்","lemma":"அனையர்","gloss":"such people"}],"gloss":"such are they"},{"surface":"வாழியோ","parts":[{"text":"வாழி","lemma":"வாழி","gloss":"may you live long"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ஓ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"may they live long"},{"surface":"இரவலர்","parts":[{"text":"இரவலர்","lemma":"இரவலர்","gloss":"suppliants"}],"gloss":"the suppliants"},{"surface":"அவரை","parts":[{"text":"அவரை","lemma":"அவர்","gloss":"them"}],"gloss":"them"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"புரவு","parts":[{"text":"புரவு","lemma":"புரவு","gloss":"patronage"}],"gloss":"patronage"},{"surface":"எதிர்கொள்ளும்","parts":[{"text":"எதிர்","lemma":"எதிர்","gloss":"welcoming"},{"text":"கொள்ளும்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"receiving"}],"gloss":"welcoming"},{"surface":"பெருஞ்செய்","parts":[{"text":"பெருஞ்செய்","lemma":"பெருஞ்செய்","gloss":"great deeds"}],"gloss":"great deeds performing"},{"surface":"ஆடவர்","parts":[{"text":"ஆடவர்","lemma":"ஆடவர்","gloss":"men"}],"gloss":"men"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உடைமை","parts":[{"text":"உடைமை","lemma":"உடைமை","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"wealth"},{"surface":"ஆகும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகும்","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"becomes"}],"gloss":"becomes"},{"surface":"அவர்","parts":[{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"அவர்","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"உடைமை","parts":[{"text":"உடைமை","lemma":"உடைமை","gloss":"wealth"}],"gloss":"wealth"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அவர்","parts":[{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"அவர்","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"இன்மை","parts":[{"text":"இன்மை","lemma":"இன்மை","gloss":"poverty"}],"gloss":"poverty"},{"surface":"ஆகும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகும்","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"becomes"}],"gloss":"becomes"},{"surface":"அவர்","parts":[{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"அவர்","gloss":"their"}],"gloss":"their"},{"surface":"இன்மையே","parts":[{"text":"இன்மை","lemma":"இன்மை","gloss":"poverty"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"poverty indeed"}]}],"literal":"In the deity-residing banyan tree's broad branches, many fruits / 'Yesterday we ate,' without thinking, again / going does not cease, the bustling flock of birds. / Such are they, may they live long, the suppliants! Them / welcoming with patronage, the men of great deeds, / their wealth becomes their wealth; / their poverty becomes their poverty.","translation":"Like the bustling flock of birds that never cease to go to the deity-residing banyan tree with broad branches and abundant fruit, never thinking, 'We ate there only yesterday,' so are the suppliants—may they live long! The wealth of the great men who welcome and patronize them is truly the suppliants' own wealth, and the poverty of those patrons is the suppliants' own poverty.","modern":"தெய்வம் உறையும் ஆலமரத்தின் பரந்த கிளைகளில் உள்ள பல பழங்களை, 'நேற்றுதான் உண்டோம்' என்று நினைக்காமல் பறவைக் கூட்டங்கள் மீண்டும் மீண்டும் தேடிச் செல்லும். இரவலர்களும் அத்தகையவர்களே; அவர்கள் வாழ்க! அவர்களை வரவேற்று ஆதரிக்கும் வள்ளல்களின் செல்வமே இரவலர்களின் செல்வமாகும்; அவ்வள்ளல்களின் வறுமையே இரவலர்களின் வறுமையுமாகும்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puram genre, under the theme of 'Parisil Kada Nilai' (demanding gifts). The poet, Perumpatumanar, compares suppliants to a flock of birds that constantly visit a fruitful banyan tree. Just as the birds do not hesitate to return to the tree day after day, forgetting that they ate there yesterday, the suppliants continuously seek out generous patrons. The poet praises these patrons, stating that their wealth is effectively the wealth of the suppliants, and their poverty is also shared by the suppliants. The key words are 'iravalar' (suppliants), 'puḷḷiṉam' (flock of birds), and 'uṭaimai' (wealth).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,2.1],[2.1,2.8],[2.98,3.5],[3.5,4.0],[4.0,4.1],[4.1,5.26],[5.26,5.38],[5.5,6.1],[6.1,6.2],[6.2,7.6],[7.6,7.7],[7.7,8.2],[8.2,8.7],[9.1,9.7],[9.7,10.1],[10.1,10.4],[10.4,10.6],[10.6,11.7],[11.7,12.1],[12.1,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,13.3],[13.3,13.6],[13.6,13.7],[13.7,14.1],[14.1,14.7]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.2],[1.2,1.74],[1.82,2.3],[2.3,3.05],[3.24,3.8],[3.8,4.3],[4.3,4.5],[4.5,5.6],[5.86,6.2],[6.2,6.7],[6.7,6.8],[6.8,8.2],[8.2,8.2],[8.2,8.9],[8.9,9.4],[9.85,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.2],[11.2,11.5],[11.5,12.9],[12.9,13.3],[13.3,13.4],[13.4,14.0],[14.0,14.7],[14.7,15.0],[15.0,15.1],[15.1,15.5],[15.5,16.2]]},"sync":[[["கடவுள்","deity-residing"]],[["ஆலத்து","of the banyan tree"],["தடவு","broad"]],[["தடவு","broad"],["சினை","branch"]],[["பல்","many"],["பழம்","fruit"]],[["நெருநல்","yesterday"]],[["உண்டனம்","we ate"]],[["என்னாது","without thinking"]],[["பின்னும்","again"]],[["செலவு","going"],["ஆனாவே","do not cease indeed"]],[["ஆனாவே","do not cease indeed"]],[["கலிகொள்","bustling"]],[["புள்ளினம்","flock of birds"]],[["அனையர்","such are they"]],[["வாழியோ","may they live long"]],[["இரவலர்","the suppliants"]],[["அவரை","them"]],[["புரவு","patronage"],["எதிர்கொள்ளும்","welcoming"]],[["எதிர்கொள்ளும்","welcoming"]],[["பெருஞ்செய்","great deeds performing"]],[["ஆடவர்","men"]],[["உடைமை","wealth"]],[["ஆகும்","becomes"]],[["அவர்","their"]],[["உடைமை","wealth"]],[["அவர்","their"]],[["இன்மை","poverty"]],[["ஆகும்","becomes"]],[["அவர்","their"]],[["இன்மையே","poverty indeed"]]]}